ceback",[234,373,374,378],{},[249,375,376],{},[202,377,337],{},[249,379,380,383],{},[202,381,382],{},"cron_failure"," events for failed scheduled jobs",[234,385,386,394],{},[249,387,388,264,391],{},[202,389,390],{},"worker.log",[202,392,393],{},"worker.error.log",[249,395,396,399],{},[202,397,398],{},"worker_failure"," events: worker crashes, OOM kills, failed jobs",[401,402,403],"note",{},[198,404,405,406,210],{},"Frappe logs \"Scheduled Job Failed\" at INFO, which the default logger drops. To catch every failing\ncron, also install the app on each site as a ",[207,407,408],{"href":41},"satellite",[212,410,412],{"id":411},"nginx-access-log","nginx access log",[198,414,415,416,264,419,264,422,425],{},"Per site and per minute of the log line's own time: ",[202,417,418],{},"http_requests",[202,420,421],{},"http_5xx",[202,423,424],{},"http_502",", plus\none aggregated event per (site, status, route) and minute. Each sample is stamped with the newest\nline of its minute, so a backlog read at once (after a restart or a rotation) lands in the minutes\nit happened, not as one spike when the agent reads it. A known site with no traffic reports zeros.",[198,427,428,429,432],{},"The site comes from ",[202,430,431],{},"$host"," when the log format includes it (a leading vhost field or a trailing\nquoted field), else from a per-site log file name, else the bench's only site.",[198,434,435,436,439,440,443,444,447],{},"The same lines feed ",[207,437,438],{"href":135},"web attack detection",": probes for secrets, admin panels,\ntraversal and injections become ",[202,441,442],{},"web_attack_probe"," events, and a secret-bearing file answered with\na 2xx becomes a critical ",[202,445,446],{},"web_sensitive_file_exposed"," event.",[212,449,451],{"id":450},"auth-log","Auth log",[198,453,218,454,264,457,460,461,464,465,264,468,264,471,474,475,264,478,264,481,264,484,487],{},[202,455,456],{},"\u002Fvar\u002Flog\u002Fauth.log",[202,458,459],{},"\u002Fvar\u002Flog\u002Fsecure",", or ",[20